/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Value Pricing is a strategy focused on maximizing the  value for customers by balancing the benefits offered against the costs. Companies often lower prices to enhance this value, ensuring that customers feel they are getting more for their money. A classic example is the Every Day Low Price \(EDLP\) model, where consistently low prices are maintained to deliver continuous value)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [7]
>>
